# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Files that are read by Linux tooling must keep LF even when checked out on
# Windows. The Docker build context is the working tree, so a CRLF shell script
# copied into an image fails with "bad interpreter", and a CRLF recipe line
# breaks GNU make. Checking out these with CRLF is a build failure, not a
# cosmetic difference.
#
# Go sources belong on that list for the same reason, one step removed. The
# toolchain runs inside a Linux container, gofmt writes LF unconditionally, and
# it rewrites in place — so with `text=auto` alone a single `make fmt` on
# Windows reports every file in the repository as modified, and `git status`
# stops being a useful signal. gofmt is the formatter of record either way.
*.go            text eol=lf
go.mod          text eol=lf
go.sum          text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.lua           text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.pdf           binary
